2... Qe7 { The queen defends e5 but blocks the f8 bishop, which makes Black's development awkward. } ( 2... Bd6 3. d4 { Takes the centre before the bishop settles. } 3... Nc6 4. dxe5 Nxe5 5. Nxe5 Bxe5 6. f4 { Kicks the bishop and gains space. } 6... Bf6 7. Bd3 ) 3. Bc4 { Develops and aims at f7. Black's queen is awkwardly placed on e7. } 3... Nf6 4. d3 { Guards e4 and opens the c1 bishop. } 4... c6 5. O-O d6 6. Nbd2 { Develops the last knight without blocking the c-pawn. Plan: c3 and a slow d4 or Nc4, and watch the e-file where the black queen can pin pieces. } *
